{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122145","id":4215587254,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc77RMG2","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122145","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122145.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122145.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122145","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122145/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122145/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122145/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c8d6e5c70760d128729a7046e8ab660646d198a3","number":122145,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Wayland: Fixing short reads and FD leaks in embedder","user":{"login":"ominousllama","id":149961466,"node_id":"U_kgDOCPA6-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149961466?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama","html_url":"https://github.com/ominousllama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ominousllama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #118212\r\n- Closes #121831\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Cause\r\n\r\nWaylandEmbedder::handle_sock() reads incoming messages assuming each read call would return exactly the number of bytes requested. Blocking SOCK_STREAM socket does not guarantee that. Kernel can sometimes hand back fewer bytes than requested. Old logic was unprepared for this case and treated it as fatal error.\r\n\r\nThe old logic also silently swallowed the issue by handle_fd() (only ERR_BUG triggered a shutdown), so the connection kept being polled afterward with its bytestream position desynced now. Next header read would then read garbage from middle of the previous message. That bad read would eventually raise a protocol error on the connection (104/ECONNRESET, 32/EPIPE, 24/EMFILE) which WaylandThread::_wl_display_check_error() treats as fatal.\r\n\r\nAlso: The EMFILE variant leads to a related bug. FDs received over the socket via SCM_RIGHTS were queued (client.fds / compositor_fds) to be claimed by a later message that needed them, but if a client disconnected (or the embedder shut down) before that followup message arrived, the queued FDs were never closed.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\n- handle_sock() reads the header and body in a single MSG_WAITALL loop that resumes from the last offset across iterations and retries on EINTR instead of treating a short read as fatal. The header is read directly rather than peeked. MSG_PEEK with MSG_WAITALL turned out to be unreliable on AF_UNIX SOCK_STREAM sockets (could return a short read that never grew -> hanging connection).\r\n- handle_fd() compositor socket logic now shuts the embedder down on any handle_sock() error (old logic just racted to ERR_BUG) since silently continuing on a desynced stream was never safe.\r\n- cleanup_socket() and shutdown() now close FDs still sitting unclaimed in client.fds / compositor_fds.\r\n- Added MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC to the body read recvmsg() so received FDs cant leak into a forked+exec child before theyre explicitly closed or handed off.\r\n\r\n## AI Disclosure\r\n\r\nLLMs were use in following area/stages:\r\n\r\n- Checking code changes for obvious bugs before submission\r\n- Additional blast-radius check of code changes\r\n- Used it to generate a few scripts used during local testing of changes","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/go